<!--
  How temperature feels and what it does (design 28 §8). CENTI-DEGREES and per-mille, like the
  rest of the thermal model.

  Four bands each side of comfort, because a colonist who is a little cold and one who is
  freezing differ in kind:

    comfortable  16–26 °C    nothing happens at all
    mild         10–16 / 26–32   mood −10, sleep ×0.90
    bad          −3–10 / 32–35   mood −50, sleep ×0.75
    extreme      below −3 / above 35   mood −120, sleep ×0.55, and severity builds

  The edges are set by the climate the meadow ships: Wash nights bottom at 10 °C and so land
  in the mild band — spring is benign, shelter wanted but not yet needed — while Hollow's
  nights cross the floor and Candle's are deep in the extreme band, where severity builds.
  Severity (hypothermia below −3 °C, heatstroke above 35 °C) mirrors starvation exactly: it
  builds by distance beyond the bound — 15 per mille per centi-degree, so a Candle night at
  −13 °C builds 15 an interval and is a full bar in four hours, and a cold snap's −33 °C fills
  it in an hour and a half — recovers by 5 anywhere inside the
  bounds, and steps condition down in the same thirds starvation does. Real lethality arrives
  with the health milestone; today it slows a colonist to the same floor. Work runs at full
  speed from 8 °C: a cold morning slows nobody, a freezing one slows everyone.
-->
<Defs>

  <TemperatureDef>
    <defName>Temperature_Colonist</defName>
    <label>colonist</label>
    <comfortMinC>1600</comfortMinC>
    <comfortMaxC>2600</comfortMaxC>
    <mildBandC>600</mildBandC>
    <coldFloorC>-300</coldFloorC>
    <hotCeilingC>3500</hotCeilingC>
    <moodMildOffset>-10</moodMildOffset>
    <moodBadOffset>-50</moodBadOffset>
    <moodExtremeOffset>-120</moodExtremeOffset>
    <sleepMildPerMille>900</sleepMildPerMille>
    <sleepBadPerMille>750</sleepBadPerMille>
    <sleepExtremePerMille>550</sleepExtremePerMille>
    <workMinC>800</workMinC>
    <workMaxC>3500</workMaxC>
    <workOutsidePerMille>700</workOutsidePerMille>
    <hypothermiaC>-300</hypothermiaC>
    <heatstrokeC>3500</heatstrokeC>
    <severitySlopePerMille>15</severitySlopePerMille>
    <severityRecoveryPerInterval>5</severityRecoveryPerInterval>
    <bodyHeatPerPass>15</bodyHeatPerPass>
    <bodyHeatGateC>4000</bodyHeatGateC>
  </TemperatureDef>

</Defs>
